# Engineering Lifecycle Gates

## Phase 1: Research & Language Selection

Entry: Requirements exist (even if rough)
Exit: Language selected, dependencies audited, rationale documented

**Gate criteria:**
- [ ] Requirements clarified
- [ ] Language selected with documented rationale (see language-selection.md)
- [ ] Key dependencies identified and audited for security/maintenance
- [ ] Existing solutions researched (no reinventing wheels)

## Phase 2: Architecture Design

Entry: Language selected, requirements clear
Exit: Plan written in `.cursor/plans/`, architecture validated

**Gate criteria:**
- [ ] Architecture pattern chosen (microservices, monolith, event-driven, etc.)
- [ ] Data model designed (entities, relationships, storage)
- [ ] API contracts defined (OpenAPI / Protobuf)
- [ ] Plan document created with approach, file manifest, test strategy, risks
- [ ] Plan approved by user

## Phase 3: Implementation

Entry: Approved plan exists
Exit: All tests pass, lint clean, coverage >= 80%

**Gate criteria:**
- [ ] TDD followed: RED (failing test) → GREEN (minimal impl) → IMPROVE (refactor)
- [ ] Lint gate: zero warnings
- [ ] Test gate: all tests pass
- [ ] Security gate: no secrets, inputs validated
- [ ] Coverage >= 80%
- [ ] Commit with conventional message

## Phase 4: Code Review

Entry: Quality gates passed, code committed
Exit: No CRITICAL or HIGH issues, reviewer approved

**Gate criteria:**
- [ ] Language-appropriate reviewer agent dispatched
- [ ] Security reviewer dispatched for auth/payments/user-data code
- [ ] All CRITICAL and HIGH issues resolved
- [ ] MEDIUM issues documented or resolved

## Phase 5: Deployment

Entry: Code reviewed and approved
Exit: Deployment verified, monitoring confirms health

**Gate criteria:**
- [ ] Docker image built with multi-stage, non-root user
- [ ] CI/CD pipeline green
- [ ] Database migration tested and reversible
- [ ] Environment variables configured in target environment
- [ ] Rollback plan documented
- [ ] Monitoring and alerting configured

## Phase 6: Maintenance

Entry: System is deployed
Exit: (ongoing — no terminal exit, but periodic checkpoints)

**Gate criteria (periodic):**
- [ ] CLAUDE.md and README.md reflect current state
- [ ] Technical debt documented in `.cursor/plans/debt.md`
- [ ] Dependencies checked for security updates
- [ ] Performance baseline re-measured

## Blocking Rules

- You CANNOT skip phases
- You CANNOT implement without an approved plan (Phase 2 exit)
- You CANNOT deploy without review approval (Phase 4 exit)
- You CANNOT bypass quality gates with "I'll fix it later"
